 const dialog=el('dialog',{className:'survey-dialog'});dialog.innerHTML=`<button class="close" aria-label="Close data notes">×</button><span class="mono" style="font-size:9px;color:#8ae5d8">OMNISCOPE / THE MEASUREMENT BEHIND THE MAP</span><h2>One scene. Different kinds of data.</h2><p><b>Solar system:</b> eight planet positions come from NASA JPL Horizons, in heliocentric Ecliptic J2000 coordinates. The initial saved epoch is 17 October 2026, 00:00 UTC. Fetch a date to query JPL. Animation propagates osculating two-body orbits from those vectors; it is a model between reference epochs. Planet radii and the SPHEREx spacecraft orbit are enlarged. Other legacy missions, moon and asteroid motions remain illustrative.</p><p><b>Infrared sky:</b> the full celestial sphere uses real 2MASS or AllWISE maps, reprojected to equatorial CAR from HiPS using CDS HiPS2FITS. The all-sky reference is clearly labeled separately from SPHEREx. The shell radius is a display choice: these are sky directions, not measured distances.</p><p><b>SPHEREx:</b> actual Level 2 spectral images are placed at their ICRS coordinates on the same sphere. Survey outlines use the archive's footprint polygons. Enter a field to inspect TAN-SIP registered observations at their true angular size. Wavelength and bandwidth come from the FITS WCS-WAVE table. The spectral window selects measured pixel wavelengths; it does not synthesize unobserved channels.</p><p><b>Comparisons:</b> A and B share a brightness stretch. A − B subtracts registered raw surface-brightness values without background, PSF, or wavelength matching; red and blue residuals are exploratory. A wavelength match indicator refers to the current aim point only. Quality-flag filtering hides pixels with any nonzero flag; interpolation can still mix neighboring pixels. Candidate notes remain local and no report is submitted to NASA.</p><p>Bundled examples are saved observations; live searches use IRSA SIA2. NASA / JPL-Caltech / Caltech / IPAC; WISE and NEOWISE are NASA-funded. This publication makes use of SPHEREx data products, a joint project of JPL and Caltech funded by NASA.</p><p><a href="https://irsa.ipac.caltech.edu/Missions/spherex.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SPHEREx archive</a> · <a href="https://ssd-api.jpl.nasa.gov/doc/horizons.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">JPL Horizons API</a> · <a href="https://alasky.cds.unistra.fr/hips-image-services/hips2fits" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CDS map projection</a></p>`;document.body.appendChild(dialog);dialog.querySelector('.close').onclick=()=>dialog.close();$('surveyMethods').onclick=()=>dialog.showModal();
